From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:26:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: share one completion notifier per submission
 (shared_notifier=1)

Metal gives each command buffer one completion notifier, shared by its
renders' TA and 3D Works and taken from a recycled pool (HV capture of
macOS 25G83, 2026-10-27: renders in one command buffer share the
notifier, renders in different ones never do). The 2026-10-03 shared
notifier was instead one per queue with a cumulative count, so the
firmware announced nothing until the whole queue drained.

Make shared_notifier=1 the Metal layout: the renders of one submission
share the notifier slot of its first published render, which writes the
header with the Work count of every render still to come in the
submission (two per render); the others write only their driver stamps.
Each render retires once the notifier's completed count reaches its
running total, as the queue-shared path did. The owner Work's storage
stays leased until the last render using its notifier retires.

The default stays 0, a notifier per render.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit ec0d1a382c8ee6c10dbfa7557a2c923aef118d58)
